/**

@page page_database Database schema

The colman database is a SQLite file with the extension `.col`
(optionally encrypted).  All tables are created when a new collection
is created, by `SQLQueries::create_tables()`
(`colman_sql_queries.cpp`).  Type-specific attribute tables are
created dynamically when a media type is created via
`SQLQueries::add_new_type()`.

When an existing file is opened, `SQLQueries::load_database()` brings
it up to date: tables and indexes that are missing are created
(`CREATE … IF NOT EXISTS`), the column `types.media_kind` is added to
older databases and filled for the predefined types
(`ensure_media_kind_column()`), and missing display names of the
predefined types are added (`ensure_predefined_translations()`).

@note SQLite only enforces foreign keys when `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`
is set.  colman therefore maintains referential integrity
programmatically in the SQL layer (`colman_sql_queries*.cpp`).  The
"FK" entries in the tables below describe the logical relations.

---

@section sec_db_overview Table overview

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `collection` | Collection-wide metadata (name, logo, barcode prefix, …) |
| `types` | Media type definitions |
| `items` | Items (books, teaching materials, CDs, …) |
| `schoolitems` | School book extension of `items` |
| `item_list_values` | Values of repeatable attribute fields |
| `items_fts` | FTS5 full-text index for the item search |
| `thumbnails` | Thumbnails (URL or local path) |
| `acquisitions` | Acquisitions (stock increase) |
| `liquidations` | Liquidations (stock decrease) |
| `persons` | Persons (borrowers and users) |
| `lendings` | Lending transactions |
| `returns` | Return transactions |
| `reservations` | Active reservations |
| `credentials` | Usernames, Argon2 password hashes and OIDC identities |
| `permissions` | Permissions per person (boolean flags) |
| `classes` | Class list of the class management |
| `translations` | Localized names of types and type fields |
| `data_types` | Data type metadata of type attributes |
| `common_field_positions` | Display position of the common fields per type |
| `signature_top_categories`, `signature_bottom_categories` | Categories for the signature (spine) labels |
| `colman_table_versions` | Change counters per table (maintained by triggers) |
| `<tablename>` | Type-specific attribute tables (dynamic) |

---

@section sec_db_collection Table: collection

Key/value store for collection-wide settings.  Each setting occupies
exactly one row.

@subsection sub_db_collection_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `key` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** | Unique identifier of the setting |
| `value` | `BLOB` | | Value of the setting (type depends on `key`) |

@subsection sub_db_collection_keys Known keys

| key | Value type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `name` | Text | Name of the collection |
| `organization` | Text | Name of the organization |
| `responsible` | Text | Responsible person |
| `barcode_prefix` | Text | Barcode prefix (5 digits, derived from name and organization) |
| `data_version` | Text | Schema version (currently `"1.0"`) |
| `max_person_id` | Integer | Highest person ID assigned so far |
| `logo` | BLOB | Raw data of the collection logo (SVG, PNG or another image format; the format is auto-detected on loading) |
| `use_lending_period` | Integer | 1 = default lending period active, 0 = none |
| `lending_period_years` | Integer | Years of the default lending period |
| `lending_period_months` | Integer | Months of the default lending period |
| `lending_period_days` | Integer | Days of the default lending period |
| `allow_reservations` | Integer | 1 = reservations allowed, 0 = disabled (default: 1) |
| `reservation_period_days` | Integer | Validity of a reservation in days (default: 14) |
| `default_item_type` | Integer | Default media type ID for new items |
| `default_is_school_item` | Integer | 1 = new items are school items by default |
| `grade_range_min` / `grade_range_max` | Integer | Range of grade levels for school items (default: 1–13) |
| `server_name` | Text | Name announced by the REST server for LAN discovery (mDNS) |

@note **Deprecated (legacy data):** the layout keys `id_card_*`,
`item_card_*`, `sig_lbl_*` as well as `id_label_layout_name` /
`item_card_label_layout_name` are **no longer written** since layouts
became client-local. Card and label layouts are stored locally per
client (desktop: `QSettings`, Flutter: `IdCardLayoutStore`). In
existing `.col` files the values remain as dead leftovers and are only
taken over once into the local presets on opening
(`migrate_card_layouts`). New databases no longer contain these keys.

Access: `create_collection()`, `change_collection()`,
`read_collection()`.

---

@section sec_db_types Table: types

Directory of all media types.

@subsection sub_db_types_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique type ID |
| `name` | `VARCHAR` | | Internal type name (e.g. `"book"`); display names are in `translations` |
| `tablename` | `VARCHAR` | | Name of the associated attribute table |
| `media_kind` | `INTEGER` | | Locale-independent kind of medium for internet lookups (`colman::MediaKind`: 0 = unknown, 1 = book, 2 = CD, 3 = DVD, 4 = Blu-ray, 5 = board game) |

New collections contain the predefined types `book`, `periodical`,
`cd`, `dvd`, `bluray` and `board_game`.

@note Creating a type also creates an attribute table `<tablename>`
and entries in `translations` and `data_types` (see `add_new_type()`).

---

@section sec_db_items Table: items

Core data of each item.  Stock and availability are maintained as
denormalized counters and updated on every mutation (acquisition,
liquidation, lending, return).

@subsection sub_db_items_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique item ID |
| `name` | `VARCHAR` | | Title of the item |
| `type` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `types.id`, index | Media type |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Total stock (acquisitions minus liquidations) |
| `available` | `INTEGER` | | Currently available (not lent) |
| `place` | `VARCHAR` | | Location |
| `description` | `VARCHAR` | | Description |
| `thumbnail` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `thumbnails.id` | Thumbnail (0 = none) |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator, NULL = unknown) |
| `signature_top` | `VARCHAR` | | Upper signature label (spine label, e.g. classification) |
| `signature_bottom` | `VARCHAR` | | Lower signature label (e.g. author abbreviation) |
| `keywords` | `VARCHAR` | | Keywords (also indexed in `items_fts`) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version (starts at 1; REST ETags) |
| `allow_reservations` | `INTEGER` | | NULL = inherit from the collection, 0 = reservations forbidden, 1 = allowed |
| `reservation_period_days` | `INTEGER` | | NULL = inherit from the collection, otherwise validity in days |

@note `count` and `available` are never computed directly via SQL
aggregates, but maintained incrementally in the mutating functions of
the SQL layer.  `available = count - (copies currently lent)`.

Access: `add_new_item()`, `get_item()`, `change_item()`,
`remove_item()`.

---

@section sec_db_schoolitems Table: schoolitems

Optional school book extension of an item.  If a row exists for an
`item_id`, the item is a school item.

@subsection sub_db_schoolitems_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `item_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK**, FK -> `items.id` | Associated item |
| `subject` | `VARCHAR` | | School subject |
| `academic_year` | `VARCHAR` | | Grade levels as an encoded string (see below) |
| `type` | `VARCHAR` | | Subtype (e.g. teacher's edition, workbook) |

@note The format of `academic_year` is a comma-separated list of
ranges: `"5-6,8"` means grades 5 to 6 and grade 8 (encoded/decoded by
`colman::academic_years_to_string()` /
`colman::string_to_academic_years()`).

---

@section sec_db_item_list_values Table: item_list_values

Stores the values of attribute fields that are marked as repeatable
(`is_repeatable = true` in `data_types.infos`).  Each row contains
exactly one value at a given position.

@subsection sub_db_item_list_values_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `item_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** (part), FK -> `items.id` | Associated item |
| `column_name` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Name of the attribute (equals the column name in the type-specific table) |
| `position` | `INTEGER` | **PK** (part) | 0-based order of the value |
| `value` | `VARCHAR` | | The actual value |

The composite primary key is `(item_id, column_name, position)`.  An
index `idx_ilv_item` on `item_id` speeds up loading all attribute
values of an item.

**Invariants:**
- For a given `(item_id, column_name)` the `position` values are
  assigned without gaps starting at 0.
- The order corresponds to the input order of the user.
- When an item is changed (`change_item`), all rows for `item_id` are
  deleted and inserted again.

---

@section sec_db_items_fts Table: items_fts

FTS5 virtual table (`tokenize='unicode61 remove_diacritics 1'`) with
the columns `name`, `description`, `keywords`, `authors`, `isbn10`,
`isbn13` and `subject`; its `rowid` is the item ID.  The SQL layer
updates the entry of an item whenever the item is created, changed or
removed.  `query_items_for_search()` uses it for the full-text search
if the table exists (SQLite builds without FTS5 fall back to `LIKE`
filters).

---

@section sec_db_thumbnails Table: thumbnails

Stores thumbnails as a URL reference or a local file path.  The image
itself is stored in the file system, not in the database.

@subsection sub_db_thumbnails_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique thumbnail ID |
| `url` | `VARCHAR` | | Source URL (empty if local) |
| `local_file` | `VARCHAR` | | Path to the local image file |

Access: `store_thumbnail()`, `get_thumbnail()`, `use_local_thumbnail()`,
`have_local_thumbnail()`.

---

@section sec_db_acquisitions Table: acquisitions

Each entry increases the stock of an item by `count` copies.

@subsection sub_db_acquisitions_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique acquisition ID |
| `item` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `items.id`, index | Affected item |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of copies acquired |
| `datetime` | `DATETIME` | | Date and time in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version |

Access: `add_new_acquisition()`, `get_acquisition()`,
`change_acquisition()`, `remove_acquisition()`.

---

@section sec_db_liquidations Table: liquidations

Each entry decreases the stock of an item by `count` copies.

@subsection sub_db_liquidations_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique liquidation ID |
| `item` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `items.id`, index | Affected item |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of copies removed |
| `datetime` | `DATETIME` | | Date and time in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version |

Access: `add_new_liquidation()`, `get_liquidation()`,
`change_liquidation()`, `remove_liquidation()`.

---

@section sec_db_persons Table: persons

Data of the persons — borrowers (pupils, teachers, …) as well as users
who log in.

@subsection sub_db_persons_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique person ID |
| `lastname` | `VARCHAR` | | Last name |
| `firstname` | `VARCHAR` | | First name |
| `title` | `VARCHAR` | | Title (e.g. `"Dr."`) |
| `school_class` | `VARCHAR` | | Class (e.g. `"3a"`; empty = no class) |
| `emails` | `VARCHAR` | | E-mail address(es), comma-separated |
| `telephonenumbers` | `VARCHAR` | | Telephone number(s) |
| `street` | `VARCHAR` | | Street address |
| `zip` | `VARCHAR` | | Postal code |
| `city` | `VARCHAR` | | City |
| `country` | `VARCHAR` | | Country |
| `remarks` | `VARCHAR` | | Remarks |
| `thumbnail` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `thumbnails.id` | Thumbnail (0 = none) |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version |

@note The person barcode is not stored in the database but computed on
demand from the person ID and the barcode prefix
(`colman::compute_person_barcode()`).

@note The row with `id = 0` is the administrator (always present,
excluded from person queries via `WHERE id > 0`).

Access: `add_new_person()`, `get_person()`, `change_person()`,
`remove_person()`.

---

@section sec_db_lendings Table: lendings

Each entry documents that a person has borrowed a number of copies of
an item.  A lending is open as long as the sum of the associated
`returns.count` values is smaller than `lendings.count`.

@subsection sub_db_lendings_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique lending ID |
| `item` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `items.id`, index | Lent item |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of copies lent |
| `person` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id`, index | Borrowing person |
| `datetime` | `DATETIME` | | Date and time of the lending in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' |
| `duedate` | `VARCHAR(10)` | | Due date `YYYY-MM-DD` (empty = none) |
| `remarks` | `VARCHAR` | | Remarks |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version |

Access: `add_new_lending()`, `get_lending()`, `change_lending()`,
`remove_lending()`, `extend_lendings()`.

---

@section sec_db_returns Table: returns

Each entry documents the (partial) return of a lending.  Several
returns per lending are allowed.

@subsection sub_db_returns_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique return ID |
| `lending` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `lendings.id`, index | Associated lending |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of copies returned |
| `datetime` | `DATETIME` | | Date and time of the return in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' |
| `remarks` | `VARCHAR` | | Remarks |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the record (0 = administrator) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version |

Access: `add_new_return()`, `get_return()`, `change_return()`,
`remove_return()`.

---

@section sec_db_reservations Table: reservations

Stores active item reservations.  Each person may create exactly one
reservation per item (UNIQUE constraint on `item_id` and `person_id`),
but the `count` column allows reserving several copies of the same
item.  The sum of all active reservations for an item must not exceed
`items.available`.

Expired reservations are cleaned up lazily: in
`get_reservations_for_item()`, `get_reservation()` and within
`add_new_lending()`, all expired entries for the item concerned are
deleted first.

@subsection sub_db_reservations_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** | Unique reservation ID |
| `item_id` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `items(id)`, index | Reserved item |
| `person_id` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons(id)`, index | Reserving person |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of reserved copies (&gt;= 1) |
| `reserved_at` | `TEXT` | | Time stamp of the reservation (ISO 8601) |
| `expires_at` | `TEXT` | | Expiry date (ISO 8601 date) |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Optimistic locking version (starts at 1) |
| `data_collector` | `INTEGER` | FK -> `persons.id` | User who entered the reservation |

Constraint: `UNIQUE(item_id, person_id)` — one person, one reservation
per item.

Access: `add_reservation()`, `remove_reservation()`,
`get_reservations_for_item()`, `get_reservation()`,
`get_reservations()`.

---

@section sec_db_credentials Table: credentials

Stores the login data of a person: username, Argon2 password hash and
external identity (OIDC subject).  Only persons with a password must
authenticate with it when opening a database file or logging in to the
REST server.  The same data is used by the desktop application and the
REST server, so the desktop password and the REST login are always in
sync.

@subsection sub_db_credentials_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `person_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK**, FK -> `persons(id)` | Associated person (0 = administrator) |
| `username` | `TEXT` | **UNIQUE** | Unique login name |
| `password_hash` | `TEXT` | | Argon2 hash of the password |
| `external_id` | `TEXT` | **UNIQUE** | OIDC subject identifier |

Password access: `set_password()`, `get_password()`, `has_password()`,
`remove_password()`, `change_own_password()`.

Username access: `get_username()`, `set_username()`,
`remove_username()`.  `set_username()` returns `false` if the chosen
name is already taken (UNIQUE constraint).

REST login: `check_local_credentials()`, `set_local_credentials()`,
`delete_local_credentials()`.

Password hashing: `colman::hash_password()` / `colman::verify_password()`
from `colman_passwords.hpp` (dependency: `libargon2`).

---

@section sec_db_permissions Table: permissions

Stores fine-grained permissions per person as boolean flags.  When the
administrator (person_id = 0) is created, all flags are set to TRUE.
New persons receive the flags of the chosen profile (see
`colman_permission_deps.hpp`); persons may only grant permissions they
hold themselves.

@subsection sub_db_permissions_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `person_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK**, FK -> `persons(id)` | Associated person (0 = administrator) |
| `edit_persons` | `BOOLEAN` | | Create, delete or change persons |
| `create_lenders` | `BOOLEAN` | | Create borrowers (restricted permissions) |
| `create_data_collectors` | `BOOLEAN` | | Create data collectors (restricted permissions) |
| `collect_lendings` | `BOOLEAN` | | Record lendings |
| `collect_returns` | `BOOLEAN` | | Record returns |
| `collect_acquisitions` | `BOOLEAN` | | Record acquisitions |
| `collect_liquidations` | `BOOLEAN` | | Record liquidations |
| `view_history` | `BOOLEAN` | | View the history |
| `view_persons` | `BOOLEAN` | | View person lists |
| `view_items` | `BOOLEAN` | | View the catalogue |
| `edit_preferences` | `BOOLEAN` | | Change the collection settings |
| `print_ids` | `BOOLEAN` | | Print ID cards |
| `print_barcodes` | `BOOLEAN` | | Print labels |
| `edit_categories` | `BOOLEAN` | | Change media types and signature categories |
| `view_personal_data` | `BOOLEAN` | | View own personal data (e.g. lendings) |
| `manage_label_layouts` | `BOOLEAN` | | Create and delete label sheet layouts |
| `calibrate_printers` | `BOOLEAN` | | Edit printer calibration settings |
| `edit_id_layout` | `BOOLEAN` | | Edit the ID card layout |
| `print_signatures` | `BOOLEAN` | | Print signature (spine) labels |
| `change_actions` | `BOOLEAN` | | Change or delete recorded actions in the history |
| `edit_program_settings` | `BOOLEAN` | | Change the program settings |
| `manage_classes` | `BOOLEAN` | | Manage classes and the school year change |
| `reserve` | `BOOLEAN` | | Reserve items for oneself (default: TRUE) |
| `edit_reservations` | `BOOLEAN` | | Create, change or delete reservations for others (default: FALSE, admin: TRUE) |
| `admin_permissions` | `BOOLEAN` | | Edit item-specific reservation settings (default: FALSE, admin: TRUE) |

@note SQLite has no native `BOOLEAN` type; the values are stored as
`INTEGER` (0 = FALSE, 1 = TRUE).

Access: `get_permissions()`, `get_user_permissions()`,
`create_default_permissions()`, `has_permission()`, `set_permission()`,
`remove_permissions()`, `is_reserve_only()`.

---

@section sec_db_classes Table: classes

Class list of the class management.  The class names offered for
persons are stored with an empty `academic_year`.

@subsection sub_db_classes_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Class name (e.g. `"10a"`) |
| `academic_year` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Academic year; currently always empty |
| `count` | `INTEGER` | | Number of pupils (currently unused) |

The composite primary key is `(name, academic_year)`.

Access: `load_class_names()`, `add_class_name()`,
`remove_class_name()`, `rename_class_name()`,
`apply_school_year_changes()`.

---

@section sec_db_translations Table: translations

Localized display names for the columns of the type-specific attribute
tables and for the type names themselves.

@subsection sub_db_translations_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tablename` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Table name (e.g. `"books"`) or `"types"` |
| `column` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Column name or type name |
| `language` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Language code (QLocale::Language as integer) |
| `name` | `VARCHAR` | | Localized display name |

The composite primary key is `(tablename, column, language)`.

Access: `get_type_locale()`, `get_type_field_label()`.

For the six predefined types and their fields,
`SQLQueries::ensure_predefined_translations()` stores German and
English display names (table `PredefinedNames` in
`colman_sql_queries_types.cpp`).  The function runs when a collection
is created and every time it is opened; it only writes missing entries
or entries that still contain the raw column name, so that names
changed by the user are kept and older collections automatically
receive the English names.

---

@section sec_db_data_types Table: data_types

Describes the data type and further parameters of each column of a
type-specific attribute table.

@subsection sub_db_data_types_schema Schema

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** (part), FK -> `types.id` | Associated media type |
| `column` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Column name in the attribute table |
| `data_type` | `INTEGER` | | Data type enum (`colman::Type::DataType`) |
| `infos` | `BLOB` | | Additional parameters as base64-encoded QDataStream (QVariantMap) |
| `position` | `INTEGER` | | Display order (default 0) |
| `marc21_tag` | `VARCHAR` | | MARC21 field designator for CSV/MARC export (empty = none) |

The composite primary key is `(type_id, column)`.

**Values of `data_type`** (enum `colman::Type::DataType`):

| Value | Name | UI element | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `String` | `QPlainTextEdit` | Multi-line text |
| 1 | `ShortString` | `QLineEdit` | Single-line text |
| 2 | `Date` | `QDateEdit` | Date |
| 3 | `Time` | `QTimeEdit` | Time |
| 4 | `Integer` | `QSpinBox` | Integer |
| 5 | `Float` | `QDoubleSpinBox` | Floating-point number |
| 6 | `Duration` | composite | Duration |
| 7 | `Table` | `QTableView` | Table |
| 8 | `IntegerRanges` | custom | Integer ranges |

**Keys in `infos`** (QVariantMap):

| Key | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `"minimum"` / `"maximum"` | `QVariant` | Optional value limits |
| `"use_minimum"` / `"use_maximum"` | `bool` | Whether the limit is active |
| `"table_info"` | serialized `KeyVector` | Column definition for `Table` fields |
| `"is_repeatable"` | `bool` | Field may occur several times (multi-value); the values are then stored in `item_list_values` |

---

@section sec_db_common_field_positions Table: common_field_positions

Display position of the common item fields (name, place, description,
…) among the type-specific fields, per type.

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK** (part), FK -> `types(id)` | Media type |
| `field` | `VARCHAR` | **PK** (part) | Name of the common field |
| `position` | `INTEGER` | | Display position |

Access: `get_combined_field_order()`, `get_default_common_field_order()`,
`save_field_order()`.

---

@section sec_db_signature_categories Tables: signature_top_categories, signature_bottom_categories

Categories offered for the upper and lower signature label.

| Table | Columns | Key |
|---|---|---|
| `signature_top_categories` | `name` | **PK** `name` |
| `signature_bottom_categories` | `top_category`, `name` | **PK** `(top_category, name)` |

`SQLQueries::seed_signature_categories()` creates the default
categories in the language of the user interface when a collection is
created (translation context `colman::SignatureCategories`).  Existing
categories are not changed.

Access: `read_signature_top_categories()`,
`add_signature_top_category()`, `remove_signature_top_category()`,
`add_signature_bottom_category()`, `remove_signature_bottom_category()`.

---

@section sec_db_table_versions Table: colman_table_versions

One change counter per table (`items`, `persons`, `lendings`,
`returns`, `acquisitions`, `liquidations`, `reservations`, `types`,
`classes`, `collection`).

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `table_name` | `TEXT` | **PK** | Name of the watched table |
| `version` | `INTEGER` | | Incremented on every change |

Triggers `tv_<table>_ins|upd|del` increment the counter after every
insert, update and delete.  `query_table_versions()` returns all
counters; clients (REST client, Flutter client) poll them to refresh
their views when other clients have changed data.

---

@section sec_db_type_tables Type-specific attribute tables

For each media type, a table with the name stored in `types.tablename`
is created when the type is created.  Its schema:

| Column | Type | Key | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `item_id` | `INTEGER` | **PK**, FK -> `items.id` | Associated item |
| `<attribute name>` | `VARCHAR` | | One attribute of the type (depending on the definition) |

Each column besides `item_id` corresponds to an entry in `data_types`
and `translations`.  The column name is normalized from the attribute
name by `string_to_column_name()` (lower case, special characters
replaced).

Fields marked as `is_repeatable = true` in `data_types.infos` do
**not** store their values in this table, but exclusively in
`item_list_values`.  The corresponding column remains `NULL`.

**Example** for the predefined type `"book"` with the table name
`"books"` (excerpt):

@code{.sql}
CREATE TABLE books (
    item_id   INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,  -- FK -> items.id
    authors   VARCHAR,
    publisher VARCHAR,
    edition   VARCHAR
);
@endcode

---

@section sec_db_relations Table relations

@code
collection        (key/value store, 1 row per setting)

types             types.id <------------------------------+
  data_types             type_id FK ----------> types.id  |
  common_field_positions type_id FK ----------> types.id  |
                                                          |
items             items.type FK -------------> types.id --+
  items.thumbnail       FK -> thumbnails.id
  items.data_collector  FK -> persons.id
  schoolitems           item_id FK -> items.id
  item_list_values      item_id FK -> items.id
  items_fts             rowid      = items.id
  <tablename>           item_id FK -> items.id
  acquisitions          item    FK -> items.id
  liquidations          item    FK -> items.id
  lendings              item    FK -> items.id
    lendings.person     FK -> persons.id
    returns             lending FK -> lendings.id
  reservations          item_id FK -> items.id
    reservations.person_id FK -> persons.id

persons           persons.id
  persons.thumbnail     FK -> thumbnails.id
  persons.school_class  ~  classes.name (by value)
  credentials           person_id FK -> persons.id
  permissions           person_id FK -> persons.id
  *.data_collector      FK -> persons.id   (all movement tables)

translations      (tablename, column, language) PK
classes           (name, academic_year) PK
signature_bottom_categories.top_category ~ signature_top_categories.name
colman_table_versions  (table_name) PK, maintained by triggers
@endcode

*/
